<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quintus Tullius Cicero</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">102–43 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Quintus Tullius <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cicero">Cicero</a> was a Roman politician and soldier, the younger brother of the orator Marcus Tullius Cicero. As one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legatus">legates</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, in 54 BCE he held his winter camp in the territory of the Nervii against a prolonged siege until Caesar relieved him. He was killed in the proscriptions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-triumvirate">Second Triumvirate</a> in 43 BCE.</p></div>
